1
00:00:00,210 --> 00:00:04,230
Hello, my name is Zogg, and I wanna welcome
you to Earthlings 101, the crash course for

2
00:00:04,230 --> 00:00:10,120
alien visitors of earth.
0:00:40.399,0:00:32.399
So, what is this course anyway? During the
course, we will discuss everything an alien

3
00:00:43,670 --> 00:00:46,379
visitor needs to know about earthlings and
their planet. No matter whether you are a

4
00:00:46,379 --> 00:00:50,739
space tourist, an alien scientist, or a galactic
conqueror: If you are interested in the human

5
00:00:50,739 --> 00:00:52,829
species, this course is for you.

6
00:00:52,829 --> 00:00:57,309
The first episode is a general introduction
into the human race, or, as they call themselves:

7
00:00:57,309 --> 00:01:00,929
Mankind. The earthlings live in a rather boring
region of the galaxy and are not particularly

8
00:01:00,929 --> 00:01:03,929
beautiful, intelligent or tasty. So, why are
they so interesting?

9
00:01:03,929 --> 00:01:07,729
Well, the earthling planet happens to be inside
a natural reservation inside a non-transit

10
00:01:07,729 --> 00:01:11,600
area inside the neutral zone between the Andromeda
Empire and the Union of Galactic Communist

11
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:15,420
Republics. Due to this position, their planet
is actually out of reach of the allmighty

12
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:19,090
and omnipresent Galactic Bureaucracy. A planetary
census alone would require more paperwork

13
00:01:19,090 --> 00:01:22,439
than the last galaxy-wide reform of the taxation
of planetary rings.

14
00:01:22,439 --> 00:01:25,810
In consequence, life on earth has developed
without any administrative supervision, wars

15
00:01:25,810 --> 00:01:29,079
and migrations don't need to be approved by
the administration, whole species can emerge

16
00:01:29,079 --> 00:01:32,799
and perish without any paperwork, and all
economical benefits stay on the planet. Earthlings

17
00:01:32,799 --> 00:01:35,320
don't even pay a tax on their moon!

18
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:38,630
The earthlings' home is a small rock called
earth, orbiting an uninteresting yellow star

19
00:01:38,630 --> 00:01:42,950
called sun. Being a tax paradise, they can
afford an enormous moon as well. The planet

20
00:01:42,950 --> 00:01:47,649
is mostly covered with hydric acid, also known
as dihydrogen-monoxyde, a slimy and disgusting

21
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:50,159
chemical which is toxic to most galactic lifeforms.

22
00:01:50,159 --> 00:01:52,960
Life on earth is roughly divided into four
kinds of creatures:

23
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:57,530
First, there are plants, greenish fiber bundles
which clamp to the ground and feed on sunlight.

24
00:01:57,530 --> 00:02:02,229
Secondly, there are animals, mobile bags filled
with red slime, which feed on plants and sometimes

25
00:02:02,229 --> 00:02:03,390
on other animals.

26
00:02:03,390 --> 00:02:07,229
Thirdly, the earthlings, pink slime bags which
feed on animals and plants and do a lot of

27
00:02:07,229 --> 00:02:09,080
weird stuff in the rest of their time.

28
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:11,380
This weird stuff is what this course is all
about.

29
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:15,000
And fourthly, there are gazillions of tiny
little creatures which feed on pretty much

30
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,090
anything else.

31
00:02:16,090 --> 00:02:19,830
However, microbes are so tiny that earthlings
can't see them with their primitive eyes.

32
00:02:19,830 --> 00:02:22,890
So the earthlings think that they are at the
end of the food chain and consider themselves

33
00:02:22,890 --> 00:02:25,970
the dominant species of the planet.

34
00:02:25,970 --> 00:02:29,430
When you visit earth, you may hear accounts
on other kinds of creatures, which feed on

35
00:02:29,430 --> 00:02:33,650
earthlings, seek moonlight, and avoid sunlight
and hydric acid. However, these creatures

36
00:02:33,650 --> 00:02:37,450
are not real - the earthlings made them up.
Making things up belongs to the weird stuff

37
00:02:37,450 --> 00:02:42,530
earthlings are used to do. We will explain
this in forthcoming episodes.

38
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:47,130
Strategic advice: As mentioned before, hydric
acid is abundant on earth. So, if you are

39
00:02:47,130 --> 00:02:50,670
planning an invasion, make sure your vessels,
battle suits and equipment are not soluble

40
00:02:50,670 --> 00:02:54,660
in hydic acid. There is nothing more embarrassing
than your mighty invasion force melting away

41
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:57,760
in a summer rain.

42
00:02:57,760 --> 00:03:02,580
Life on earth is all about three things: Feeding,
reproducing and not dying - which is kind

43
00:03:02,580 --> 00:03:06,540
of redundant, as feeding is all about not
dying, and reproducing and not dying are all

44
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:09,060
about not letting the genetic code die.

45
00:03:09,060 --> 00:03:12,700
The genetic code is a quaternary code written
on tiny molecules and stored inside the elementary

46
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:17,040
building blocks of their bodies. It defines
the creature's appearance, ability and behaviour,

47
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:20,500
and the most successful codes are those who
make their creatures protect and spread the

48
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:26,230
code. In other words: Feeding, reproducing
and not dying.

49
00:03:26,230 --> 00:03:29,630
With time, animals developed a whole lot of
tricks in order to get better and better at

50
00:03:29,630 --> 00:03:34,090
feeding, reproducing and not dying: Natural
weapons, size, useless but attractive antlers

51
00:03:34,090 --> 00:03:39,620
or feathers, speed, protective shells, camouflage,
the ability to climb or even to fly. But when

52
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:43,840
it came to creating the earthlings, nature
got lazy and gave them none of this. Instead,

53
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:47,170
she just gave them a brain and told them to
figure everything out for themselves.

54
00:03:47,170 --> 00:03:51,410
Which they did. Remarkably well, by the way.
The trick was to replace the missing natural

55
00:03:51,410 --> 00:03:56,370
attributes by self-made ones, which they called
"tools". With these tools, earthlings could

56
00:03:56,370 --> 00:03:59,680
adapt better to any given circumstances than
any other species on the planet.

57
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:04,370
Except for the microbes.

58
00:04:04,370 --> 00:04:09,120
Tips for tourists: A vacation on earth may
be exciting, but it can also be very expensive.

59
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:12,170
If you are low on budget and only want to
spend the weekend, why not take a trip to

60
00:04:12,170 --> 00:04:15,860
the moon? It's not overcrowded, you'll have
a great view on earth, and you might even

61
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:17,810
stumble upon some human artefacts.

62
00:04:17,810 --> 00:04:23,409
One of the best ways to keep eating, reproducing
and not dying is actually killing. Earthlings

63
00:04:23,409 --> 00:04:26,979
are real experts on killing. Mankind is the
only galactic civilization that invented the

64
00:04:26,979 --> 00:04:32,629
hydrogen bomb before the teleportation device.
Earthlings kill plants for food, animals for

65
00:04:32,629 --> 00:04:36,460
more food, rival earthlings to get their food
and reproduction partners, and microbes not

66
00:04:36,460 --> 00:04:38,539
to be killed by them.

67
00:04:38,539 --> 00:04:41,770
Earthlings have even found a use for the inedible
parts of plants and animals they killed: They

68
00:04:41,770 --> 00:04:45,789
wrap them around their bodies. This is called
"clothing". Having sophisticated clothing

69
00:04:45,789 --> 00:04:48,849
is something that attracts more potential
reproduction partners, which may then lead

70
00:04:48,849 --> 00:04:50,569
to more killing.

71
00:04:50,569 --> 00:04:53,849
To prevent earthlings from killing each other
up to the last earthling standing, they have

72
00:04:53,849 --> 00:04:57,680
developed something called society. Earthlings
usually think that society is a big group

73
00:04:57,680 --> 00:05:02,800
of humans, but actually it's more of an abstract
entity. Society isn't something that actually

74
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:06,319
exists, but that doesn't hinder it from having
a strong opinion on pretty much anything.

75
00:05:06,319 --> 00:05:10,300
It tells earthlings what to do, what not to
do, what to eat, what tools to use, whom to

76
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:14,340
reproduce with and what cloth to wear. Society
basically imposes on earthlings the interest

77
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:18,099
of the group, pretty much like the genetic
code imposes its own interest.

78
00:05:18,099 --> 00:05:22,289
The earthlings didn't actually invent society
- it developed with mankind. Society is kind

79
00:05:22,289 --> 00:05:26,370
of hardwired into their brain. See, in the
center of the human mind is the Ego, the part

80
00:05:26,370 --> 00:05:30,479
that observes the world and decides what to
do. But the Ego isn't alone. It's based upon

81
00:05:30,479 --> 00:05:33,860
a dark and strange part we might call the
Beast, which defends the interest of the genetic

82
00:05:33,860 --> 00:05:37,050
code: Feeding, reproducing and not dying.

83
00:05:37,050 --> 00:05:39,849
On the other hand we have what we might call
the Niggler, which is kind of an advocate

84
00:05:39,849 --> 00:05:43,680
of society. Whereas the Beast tells the Ego
what he would like to do, the Niggler keeps

85
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:48,389
telling him what he should do. The Ego is,
so to say, slave of two masters. Whereas the

86
00:05:48,389 --> 00:05:52,310
Beast tries to control him with things like
pleasure, fear, desire and pain, the Niggler

87
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:56,360
manipulates him with things like remorse and
the feeling of success. As the former one

88
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:59,449
represents the needs of the code, and the
latter one the interests of the group, both

89
00:05:59,449 --> 00:06:03,379
often disagree. The Ego passes most of his
time navigating between the demands and interdictions

90
00:06:03,379 --> 00:06:08,150
of both parties - a process called, rather
incorrectly, "free will".

91
00:06:08,150 --> 00:06:12,830
Scientific advice: When you experiment on
earthlings, don't try to separate the three

92
00:06:12,830 --> 00:06:17,110
parts of the brain by surgery. That's not
possible, as they are all tangled together.

93
00:06:17,110 --> 00:06:21,139
Instead, try stimulating different parts of
the brain with electric shocks and see what

94
00:06:21,139 --> 00:06:23,349
happens. This is an interesting and entertaining
way of learning about the functions of the

95
00:06:23,349 --> 00:06:28,990
brain. It's also a great science fair project
for young scientists.

96
00:06:28,990 --> 00:06:32,319
The funny thing is that neither the Beast
nor the Niggler seem to live in the present.

97
00:06:32,319 --> 00:06:35,710
The Beast still lives in a distant past where
life was tough, rules were simple, killing

98
00:06:35,710 --> 00:06:39,330
was a necessity, reproducing didn't follow
any rules, eating involved a lot of running

99
00:06:39,330 --> 00:06:42,759
after animals, and not dying involved a lot
of running from predators.

100
00:06:42,759 --> 00:06:46,610
The Niggler, on the other hand, lives sometimes
in an idealized future where life is easy,

101
00:06:46,610 --> 00:06:50,460
nobody kills anybody anymore, everybody is
kind and perfect and everything will be better.

102
00:06:50,460 --> 00:06:54,909
Sometimes, however, the Niggler lives in an
equally idealized, not-so-distant past, where

103
00:06:54,909 --> 00:06:58,610
rules were strict, manners were different,
clothing covered more skin, reproducing was

104
00:06:58,610 --> 00:07:00,169
nearly prohibited and everything was better.

105
00:07:00,169 --> 00:07:04,259
So, the Ego, having to deal with the present,
has sometimes a hard time reuniting the wishes

106
00:07:04,259 --> 00:07:05,770
of his two masters.

107
00:07:05,770 --> 00:07:09,729
This was the first episode of Earthlings 101.
In forthcoming episodes, I will tell you more

108
00:07:09,729 --> 00:07:14,199
about evolution and society, but also about
weird things like nations, myths, dreams,

109
00:07:14,199 --> 00:07:18,719
sex, magic, rituals, beauty, money, games
and much more.

110
00:07:18,719 --> 00:07:22,539
Next time you will learn about evolution,
genetics, and why the genetic code of earthlings

111
00:07:22,539 --> 00:07:26,620
contains the sentence "Squids are stupid"
an an ancient Sagittarian dialect.

112
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:33,620
Thank you for watching!

